      "text": "$A$ is the area of the hexagon, $B$ is the area of the three rectangles formed. Note that $z = \\frac{1}{w}$ where $w$ is real, so $B = A + 2B_r$, solving $2B_r = 8B$, $B_r = 4B$. Alternatively, $z = x+iy$ where $x,y\\in[0,1]$, so $B_r = B\\pi$ and since $B = A + 2B_r$, $B = \\frac{6\\pi}{6} = \\pi$.\n\nI nearly gave away my answer with just two errors.",
